Before running:
- All output files are located in the selected directory, in the folder named Results.
Make sure there is no other folder named Results in your selected directory, as it may be overwritten.
- To make inputs static, File_Importer.py line 143 has all manipulable inputs listed. Change values within parentheses.
- for convenience, can set directory for file selection on line 157. Default directory is location of the code.

To run, navigate with cd to the folder the codes are in, and type python code_name.py in the terminal.
The code we run is CV_Loop, the rest are functions it needs.

plug and run:
- if using anaconda, pip install PyQt6 through conda console before running. If not, may need to install all packages through cmd.
- all functions used here are core to the packages and should not deprecate soon.

Warning:
- multiple file selection only works if files are in one directory
- code only works with starvation intervals
- FRET mode not implemented



Dependencies:
Python 3.12.4
PyQt 6.8.1
numpy 1.26.4
polars 1.26
matplotlib 3.8.4
scipy 1.13.1

if starts deprecating:
- install pyenv (for macOS/linux: pip install pyenv, for windows follow
https://github.com/pyenv-win/pyenv-win/blob/master/docs/installation.md#powershell)

- navigate to the folder you wish to use for this code

- give in pyenv local 3.12 (sets the python version of this directory (without parent or children) to 3.12).
If you do not have python 3.12, install by pyenv install 3.12, and then set the version.

- set up a venv: python -m venv

- paste in all the files in this code to that directory

- install the dependencies mentioned